from write_dossiers import add
add('gaussianmap',year=2025,venue='ICCV 2025',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],
problem='Represent both geometry and open-set semantics for discrete VLN. Requires panoramic RGB-D, camera intrinsics/poses and graph candidate nodes; 3D representation alone does not turn this into continuous control.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3 pp3–5): back-project depth pixels to pseudo-lidar points, initialize anisotropic Gaussians with position, covariance, opacity and color, then refine through differentiable RGB/depth rendering. SAM2 masks identify coherent regions; CLIP produces512-D region embeddings, mean-pooled to one scalar per region. A rendered scalar semantic attribute on each Gaussian is optimized to match these targets. Action features concatenate3-D position,3-D color and1-D semantic code into7-D vectors. Scene-wide, view-restricted and instance-restricted pooling feed language-conditioned transformer heads; map their scores to candidate waypoints and combine with traditional2D action scores and topological memory. Navigation pretrains MLM/SAP/OG, then DAgger; map optimization uses RGB L1/SSIM, depth L1 and semantic L1. Reported100k pretrain iterations batch64,25k finetuning batch8; inference constructs map at each waypoint. Claimed0.07s map construction is author-reported and should not be conflated with total SAM2/CLIP/navigation latency.',
novelty='Explicit Gaussian geometry plus semantic grouping and scene/view/instance action heads, relative to VER voxels and BEVBert top-down cells. It reuses a DUET-referenced topological/decision framework rather than establishing a wholly independent architecture (§3.5).',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: Table2 p6 reports R2R test75 SR/65 SPL, versus BEVBert73/62; REVERIE Table1 val-unseen53.59 SR/26.74 RGSPL and test52.93/25.76. Test navigation SR is below some contemporary methods even when grounding improves. The evidence supports task utility, not retention of arbitrary CLIP semantics. DEDUCTION: mean-pooling a512-D embedding is non-injective, so distinct vectors can share the same semantic scalar. Eq12 sums three normalized distributions but labels the result [0,1]; absent normalization it need not be a probability distribution. This notation/implementation ambiguity cannot be resolved without code.',
implementation='Official pinned repository contains README only; no released mapping, semantic compression, loss or action-fusion code was available to verify equations or latency accounting.',repository_status='Official README-only snapshot',
bottlenecks=[{'description':'Open-set scalar semantic compression irreversibly discards distinctions; test with pairs of regions with equal/near-equal feature mean but different navigation relevance. UAGM changes semantic representation/uncertainty, but released implementation is also unavailable.','evidence':'AUTHOR Eq7–8 p4; DEDUCTION','kind':'methodological','status':'Uncertain because evidence is insufficient','followups':['UAGM'],'confidence':'high for information loss, unknown behavioral impact'}, {'description':'RGB-D/pose assumptions and segmentation/rendering overhead remain; no observed closed-loop physical robot robustness established by discrete benchmark gains.','evidence':'AUTHOR task §3 and runtime §3.5','kind':'insufficiently tested','status':'Still unresolved in reviewed evidence','followups':['GA-VLN'],'confidence':'medium'}],followups=['https://github.com/Gaozzzz/Uncertainty-Aware-VLN'])
add('uagm',year=2026,venue='ICLR 2026 (PDF header)',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10],
problem='Use spatially localized uncertainty to guide RGB-D graph navigation under ambiguous geometry, semantics and appearance. Requires differentiable Gaussian reconstruction and known camera transforms; does not directly estimate calibrated action-error probabilities.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3 pp4–6): Semantic Gaussian Map initializes position3, scale3, quaternion4, opacity1, color3 and semantic3 attributes. Prune small/transparent Gaussians. Learn variational position/scale perturbations with an ELBO under Gaussian position and scale-relative uniform priors; aggregate posterior standard deviations for geometric uncertainty. Repeat for semantic offsets. Appearance score is logdet of each Gaussian block of an image-reconstruction Fisher/Gauss–Newton approximation (Eq9). Concatenate three uncertainty scalars with17 original attributes into20-D Gaussian vectors, project to768 dimensions, aggregate and fuse with instruction through transformer action scores/topological memory. Pretrain MLM/SAP/OG100k iterations batch64, Adam1e-4; DAgger25k batch8 LR1e-5. Inference reconstructs map and uncertainty before predicting action.',
novelty='Extends Gaussian scene representations with separate geometry/semantic perturbation variability and appearance sensitivity. Table4 compares DUET, geometry-only, uncertainty-only and joint representations; Table6 ablates uncertainty components. This is uncertainty-informed representation learning, not a proven Bayesian navigation policy.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: R2R Table2 p8 gives test76 SR/66 SPL, equal to VER in these rounded metrics; val-unseen78/66. Table4 p9 lists REVERIE full-model SR53.37, whereas headline Table1 p7 lists56.37 with the same37.65 RGS/27.01 RGSPL; preserve this internal discrepancy rather than choosing one silently. Table5 pruning increases FPS from11.2 to15.5 at42k primitives, but aggressive35k harms SR. DEDUCTION: logdet Fisher can be negative or−∞ and is a sensitivity/precision quantity; interpreting it as nonnegative uncertainty-ellipsoid volume requires qualifications, regularization and possibly inverse information. Eq8 approximation also requires small residuals. No calibration/error-prediction experiment in inspected tables establishes that higher score means larger decision error.',
implementation='Pinned official tree has only README; cannot inspect damping, singular-block handling, semantic embedding reduction, uncertainty gradient estimation or exact benchmark settings. No code execution.',repository_status='Official README-only snapshot',
bottlenecks=[{'description':'Calibration and numerical interpretation of appearance uncertainty are unverified: Fisher sensitivity is not posterior covariance without extra assumptions. A scalar uncertainty controller should not treat these features as probabilities.','evidence':'AUTHOR Eqs8–9 p5; DEDUCTION','kind':'methodological','status':'Still unresolved in reviewed evidence','followups':[],'confidence':'high for mathematical caveat'}, {'description':'Reconstruction uncertainty can reflect texture/surface sensitivity rather than task-relevant ambiguity; test equal-compute selective sensing or wrong-action prediction before claiming active information gathering.','evidence':'DEDUCTION from unsupervised rendering scores vs task policy; Table6 only aggregate navigation','kind':'insufficiently tested','status':'Uncertain because evidence is insufficient','followups':['active perception / world-model evaluators'],'confidence':'medium'}],limitations='No implementation released in pinned tree. Table1 versus Table4/6 REVERIE SR discrepancy remains unresolved. Figures show qualitative cases but do not establish physical collision avoidance on the discrete benchmark.')
add('bevbert',year=2023,venue='ICCV 2023',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],authors=['Dong An','Yuankai Qi','Yangguang Li','Yan Huang','Liang Wang','Tieniu Tan','Jing Shao'],title='BEVBert: Multimodal Map Pre-training for Language-guided Navigation',
problem='Panorama-only pretraining duplicates observations and makes local spatial relations implicit. BEVBert combines a global topology with a fine local ground-plane representation, assuming depth and pose or estimated depth.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3): CLIP patch features projected using depth/pose into a21×21 metric grid of0.5m cells, centered on the current agent; aggregate nearby visited nodes within a topology-order neighbourhood. Keep global visited/current/ghost graph nodes with panorama features. DUET-style graph-aware attention handles topology; a second cross-modal transformer handles cell features with polar location and navigability embeddings. Hybrid single-action prediction maps local cells to global node scores and gates local/global outputs (Eqs3–5). MLM predicts masked words; masked semantic imagination (MSI) predicts40-category multilabel semantics in masked cells with binary cross entropy (Eq6). MSI is a training auxiliary, not an online future-state rollout. Alternate teacher/student forcing after pretraining. Pretrain100k batch64 then finetune40k batch16,4 A100s, respectively about10/20hours. CE variant adds waypoint prediction and topology construction.',
novelty='Joint local metric/global topological pretraining, spatial embeddings and MSI. It explicitly inherits DUET GASA; hybrid representation differs from simply appending raw depth. Table5 compares topology, metric and hybrid maps under sensed/estimated depth.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: R2R Table1 p6 test73 SR/62 SPL versus DUET69/59. REVERIE test52.81 SR/22.09 RGSPL is nearly DUET52.51/22.06 despite larger validation gains. Table5 p7 hybrid estimated-depth74.67 SR/63.63 SPL versus sensed74.88/63.60 suggests exact depth is not essential on that test. Fig4 spatial/numerical-token slices degrade with increasing complexity even for BEVBert. Verdict: improves spatial representation, while complexity-conditioned language understanding remains partial; leaderboard comparisons must control CLIP, augmentation and sensor interfaces.',
implementation='INSPECTED CODE confirms depth-to-world projection, local BEV embeddings and cross-entropy fused action losses. Inspected CE pretraining source hard-codes bev_dim=11 (vilmodel.py715), whereas paper general/discrete setting describes21; this is a variant/config difference requiring explicit reconciliation, not automatically a bug.',
code=[{'path':'bevbert_ce/pretrain/pretrain_src/model/bev_utils.py','locator':'pixel_to_world_mapping200;PointCloud.forward349;project_bev382','finding':'depth/pose projection and BEV pooling'}, {'path':'bevbert_ce/pretrain/pretrain_src/model/vilmodel.py','locator':'LocalBEVEncoder581–609;GlocalTextPathCMT712–730','finding':'cell embedding and CE grid setting'}, {'path':'bevbert_ce/pretrain/pretrain_src/model/pretrain_cmt.py','locator':'347–350','finding':'global/local/fused action cross-entropy losses'}],
bottlenecks=[{'description':'Fixed local metric extent limits detailed memory of distant regions; GridMM keeps global history but dynamic rescaling sacrifices resolution as coverage expands.','evidence':'AUTHOR §3.1; GridMM §3.2','kind':'methodological','status':'Shifted into another cost or limitation','followups':['GridMM','VER','GA-VLN'],'confidence':'high'}, {'description':'MSI fills masked semantic cells without proving action-conditioned future prediction or calibrated uncertainty; unseen-region hallucination remains insufficiently tested.','evidence':'AUTHOR Eq6; DEDUCTION','kind':'insufficiently tested','status':'Partially addressed','followups':['HNR','UAGM'],'confidence':'medium'}])
add('gridmm',year=2023,venue='ICCV 2023',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7,8],
problem='Retain global spatial relationships across previously visited observations without collapsing history to recurrence or restricting geometric reasoning to a local metric window. Uses RGB-D, pose and panoramic observations; CE uses pretrained waypoint proposals.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3 pp4–6): store CLIP-B/32 grid features with absolute projected coordinates. At every action rotate/translate all history to the current egocentric frame. Set square extent to twice the maximum absolute coordinate and divide into fixed N×N cells. Within each cell, score feature-token relevance, max over instruction words, softmax over features, and weighted-pool into a768-D cell token (Eqs6–10). Combine map and trajectory memories, then cross-attend observation/history queries to instruction/history/map features. DUET-style dynamic fusion scores local views and global waypoints. Pretrain MLM/MVM/SAP plus historical-environment reasoning (HER), which predicts action without current panorama; DAgger uses graph shortest-route pseudo-expert. Inference retains all historical feature/coordinate pairs, so fixed map tokens do not mean fixed raw-history memory.',
novelty='Compared with BEVBert, global rather than local metric coverage and instruction-conditioned per-cell pooling; compared with DUET, explicit continuous geometry and history-only auxiliary prediction. HER is not a learned future simulator.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: Table2 p7 R2R test73 SR/62 SPL. CE Table4 p8 contrasts shared-waypoint DUET42/36 test with GridMM46/39. Table5 CE map ablation49.05 SR/40.99 SPL versus no-map45.19/37.82. Table7 increases N from8 to14 to20 and SPL39.49→40.99→42.52, exposing a resolution/compute tradeoff. Main discrete/CE scores should not be merged: camera90-degree versus panoramic and waypoint availability differ explicitly in Table4 footnote.',
implementation='INSPECTED CODE: CE GridMap stores geometry and constructs maps in getGlobalMap, and model forward_navigation_per_step consumes grid features/indexes alongside graph/observation embeddings. The CE implementation adds local/global logits on candidate space; do not assume exact discrete global-action semantics from this branch alone.',
code=[{'path':'VLN_CE/vlnce_baselines/models/Policy_ViewSelection_GridMap.py','locator':'get_rel_position1263;get_gridmap_pos_fts1321;getGlobalMap1377','finding':'depth-driven map construction'}, {'path':'VLN_CE/vlnce_baselines/models/gridmap/vilmodel.py','locator':'forward_navigation_per_step1419–1595','finding':'map-conditioned action path and local/global masked logits'}],
bottlenecks=[{'description':'Fixed cell count with expanding physical extent merges increasingly distant objects into cells; raw history grows with steps. Long-horizon gains must be evaluated against both spatial resolution and cumulative memory.','evidence':'AUTHOR Eqs2–4; Table7; DEDUCTION','kind':'methodological','status':'Partially addressed','followups':['VER','3D Gaussian Map'],'confidence':'high'}, {'description':'Instruction-max relevance pooling can suppress evidence for negation/order when salient nouns dominate; no counterfactual grounding experiment in inspected ablations establishes compositional fidelity.','evidence':'DEDUCTION Eqs6–9','kind':'insufficiently tested','status':'Uncertain because evidence is insufficient','followups':['NavNuances'],'confidence':'medium'}])
add('kerm',year=2023,venue='CVPR 2023',pages=[1,3,4,5,6,7],
problem='Augment DUET view/history features with relational descriptions not explicit in holistic visual embeddings. Discrete panoramic graph navigation, with object boxes/detector required for grounding tasks.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3 pp3–5): normalize Visual Genome attribute-object and subject-predicate-object phrases into630k unique facts. Crop each panorama view into5 regions; retrieve top5 facts per region by CLIP cosine similarity, producing25 fact tokens/view. Instruction-token dot products followed by row max score relevance; purify facts, visual regions and history. Two-layer cross-modal fact attention enhances view/history features, instruction-CLS-guided attention pools subregions, FFN combines them, then DUET predicts global action and object. Train MLM, masked-view classification, SAP and optional OG; finetune with pseudo-expert IL. R2R pretraining200k and finetuning20k iterations on4 RTX3090s; REVERIE100k/20k. Retrieval uses external Visual Genome/CLIP priors, not verified facts guaranteed true in the current scene.',
novelty='Knowledge retrieval plus instruction-conditioned purification and separate fact interactions, atop DUET. Table4 isolates modules; Table5 compares relation facts with5 detected object labels embedded through the same text encoder.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: Table2 p7 R2R test KERM69.73 SR/59.25 SPL versus reproduced DUET69.25/58.68: modest gain. REVERIE Table1 test KERM52.43 SR/39.21 SPL versus DUET52.51/36.06: efficiency improves while SR slightly drops. Table5 val-unseen facts50.44 SR/35.38 SPL versus object labels49.73/33.95. Verdict: relational feature utility is supported, but broad claims of universally better navigation should respect dataset and metric differences.',
implementation='INSPECTED CODE confirms knowledge/crop/instruction/history inputs to panorama encoding and inherited graph/local masking. Retrieval and knowledge-base parsing scripts exist; their downloaded snapshots preserve the preprocessing pathway. No timing, factuality or full reproduction executed.',
code=[{'path':'knowledge_nav_src/models/vilmodel.py','locator':'forward_panorama_per_step1465–1467;forward_navigation_per_step1747;masking1823–1833','finding':'knowledge-conditioned DUET pipeline'}, {'path':'preprocess/retrieve_facts.py','locator':'FeaturesDB22–28','finding':'HDF5 feature loading for retrieval'}, {'path':'preprocess/get_knowledge_base.py','locator':'VisualGenomeCaptions15–21','finding':'Visual Genome annotation parsing'}],
bottlenecks=[{'description':'CLIP top-k retrieval supplies plausible but unverified region facts. Instruction-aware filtering measures relevance, not truth; wrong relationships can be amplified.','evidence':'AUTHOR §3.2–3.3; DEDUCTION','kind':'methodological','status':'Partially addressed','followups':['OVER-NAV','NavRAG','UAGM'],'confidence':'medium'}, {'description':'Five crops×five facts×36 views increases representation/preprocessing load; no matched-latency baseline in inspected main tables isolates utility per compute.','evidence':'AUTHOR representation counts; DEDUCTION','kind':'insufficiently tested','status':'Uncertain because evidence is insufficient','followups':[],'confidence':'medium'}])
add('ver',year=2024,venue='CVPR 2024',pages=[1,3,4,5,6],
problem='Preserve vertical geometry and scene semantics lost by panorama and top-down summaries. Assumes calibrated multi-view images and Manhattan-style room layouts; trains with derived3D occupancy, layout and object annotations.',
method='AUTHOR METHOD (§3 pp3–6): learned3D queries project into2D feature maps through deformable cross-view attention; cascade3D deconvolution/refinement grows15×15×4 initial queries to fine volume. Occupancy focal loss, layout L1/IoU and3D detection matching losses jointly pretrain geometry (weights2,.25,.25). Freeze this encoder for navigation. Height-sliced shared transformers combine instruction with voxel tokens, predict a3D state distribution, average over height, integrate around candidate nodes and normalize to local actions. Pooled candidate pillars form global episodic graph nodes; mix graph action scores with local/backtrack scores. Navigation uses heatmap focal supervision locally, CE globally, MLM/SAP/OG pretraining100k batch64 and DAgger20k batch8. Reported training8×24GB RTX4090. Fine labels cover120×120×35 cells at0.1m. Predicting volume state is action scoring, not a learned action-conditioned environment rollout.',
novelty='Coarse-to-fine volumetric representation and3D task supervision, compared with2D metric maps, plus local volume/global graph decision fusion. Extra3D supervision is part of the contribution and a confounder when asserting architecture-only gains.',
results='PAPER EXPERIMENT: Table1 p6 test R2R76 SR/66 SPL versus BEVBert73/62 and DUET69/59. Additional dense-label generation uses existing MP3D LiDAR labels, so “no additional human annotation” does not mean no additional privileged supervision. Verdict: stronger3D representation, but freezing a scene encoder and assuming Manhattan geometry restricts adaptation to changing/non-Manhattan scenes. Height grouping reduces full volumetric attention cost while limiting direct cross-height interactions.',
implementation='Official repository tree and README were inspected, but navigation-specific source was not located among the sampled repository paths; repository contains3D detection/configuration infrastructure. No claimed DUET inheritance beyond paper-described architectural similarity is made. Exact navigation training/evaluation release completeness remains an access gap.',
bottlenecks=[{'description':'Volumetric resolution, labeling and feature storage cost scale with XYZ; height grouping reduces attention coupling but does not make dense voxels free. Gaussian maps target compact/sparse geometry but add reconstruction costs.','evidence':'AUTHOR §3.1–3.5; DEDUCTION','kind':'methodological','status':'Shifted into another cost or limitation','followups':['3D Gaussian Map','UAGM'],'confidence':'high'}, {'description':'Manhattan layout and static frozen geometry supervision are untested under pose drift, movable objects and non-Manhattan scenes in the inspected navigation table.','evidence':'AUTHOR assumptions §3; DEDUCTION','kind':'insufficiently tested','status':'Still unresolved in reviewed evidence','followups':['GA-VLN sensor noise'],'confidence':'medium'}])
